<h2 id="calc">Price calculation</h2>
<pre><span class="c">1 — rooms from the selected arrangement</span>
  for each selected rate row:
      rate = price_per_night[room_type][guests_in_row]
      <span class="c">a child is priced from its age band, not the adult column</span>
  <span class="y">Package Price</span> = Σ(rate × quantity) × nights

<span class="c">2 — included, contribute zero, always shown</span>
  breakfast · taxes-in-rate · transfers        <span class="g">→ inclusions strip</span>

<span class="c">3 — selected add-ons</span>
  per_person       → price × guests × nights   <span class="c">dinner, lunch</span>
  per_person_once  → price × guests            <span class="c">railway</span>
  per_unit         → price × quantity          <span class="c">VIP car, ZamZam room, extra nights</span>

<span class="c">4 — totals</span>
  base  = Package Price + Σ(add-ons) − Discount
  <span class="y">TAX</span>   = base × 15%                         <span class="p">← see question 4</span>
  <span class="y">Total Include vat</span> = base + TAX
  per_person_display = Total ÷ guests          <span class="c">display only, never stored</span></pre>

<div class="note warn">
  <b>Two requirements on the back end</b>
  <p><strong>Recalculation is server-side.</strong> Client-side arithmetic will eventually disagree with the payment total, and the traveller will see one number then be charged another.</p>
  <p><strong>Availability is checked at selection, not only at Proceed.</strong> If the Triple sells out while the traveller assembles, that row must grey out with a reason — not fail at payment.</p>
</div>

